# Repo documentation, not a dotfile. Without this, chezmoi treats it as a
# target for ~/README.md and reports it perpetually missing; `chezmoi forget`
# is the wrong fix because it would delete the file the GitHub repo renders.
README.md

# Claude Code rewrites this file itself, including an autoMode.environment
# block describing the local security posture (secrets tooling, CI secret
# names, repo paths). This repo is public, so that block must not be tracked,
# and stripping it by hand does not hold — Claude Code regenerates it. The
# rest of ~/.claude (skills, hooks, statusline, themes) stays managed.
.claude/settings.json
